{%- comment -%}
  One card in the #blocks band, rendered once per flavour. The band is
  two products -- Sushi Blocks (SKU 565) and Ice Cream Blocks (SKU 568)
  -- that are the same kinetic fidget in different foods, so they share
  a heading and a shape and differ only in photo, name, price and copy.

  Everything that differs comes in as a parameter. The product is looked
  up here from the handle rather than passed in, because a snippet
  cannot see variables the section assigned. Same arrangement as
  snippets/wt-new.liquid, for the same reason.

  Shaped like the bubble cards rather than the wide wt-new card: photo
  on top, then name and price on one line, copy, and the button. Two of
  those sit side by side at the width one wt-new card needs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% assign blocks_product = all_products[handle] %}
<article class="wt-blocks__card">
  <div class="wt-blocks__media">{% if blocks_product.featured_image %}<img src="{{ blocks_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }}" width="{{ blocks_product.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ blocks_product.featured_image.height }}" alt="{{ blocks_product.title }}" class="wt-blocks__img">{% else %}{% render 'wt-img', img: fallback_image, label: fallback_label, fit: 'contain' %}{% endif %}</div>
  <div class="wt-blocks__body">
    <div class="wt-blocks__row">
      <h3 class="wt-blocks__name">{{ name }}</h3>
      <span class="wt-blocks__price">{{ blocks_product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%}
      The band eyebrow says "just landed" for both cards, so a card that
      cannot actually be bought has to say so itself -- the stacked
      bands it replaced each carried their own availability in the
      eyebrow, and that promise should not be lost to the merge. Only
      the unbuyable case prints: "available now" under every card that
      is simply in stock would be noise on a page that says it once.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% unless blocks_product.available %}<span class="wt-blocks__meta">Coming soon</span>{% endunless %}
    <p class="wt-blocks__copy">{{ copy }}</p>
    <a href="{{ blocks_product.url }}" class="wt-blocks__cta">{{ cta }}</a>
  </div>
</article>
